# Dual-use disclosure

Packages: socket, @socketsecurity/cli, @socketsecurity/cli-with-sentry
Content policy class: dual-use (https://docs.npmjs.com/policies/dual-use)

## Dual-use functionality

These packages build from one source and ship the `socket`, `socket-npm`,
and `socket-npx` executables, which wrap and shim other package managers,
intercept dependency installation, scan dependency trees and package
contents, and report findings to the socket.dev security API.
Package-manager shimming, install interception, and bulk package inspection
are behaviors that can resemble malicious software to automated scanning.

## Intended legitimate use

Defensive supply-chain security analysis for developers and CI: surfacing
known-malicious, hijacked, typosquatted, or policy-violating dependencies
before they run, and providing socket.dev scan results from the command line.
The packages provide no exploitation, persistence, exfiltration, or
obfuscation capability, and transmit only the package identifiers and scan
artifacts needed for analysis. Source and issue tracker:
https://github.com/SocketDev/socket-cli
